.TH CLRU_INIT 3 "2026-08-02" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clru_init \- initialise a previously declared LRU cache variable
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clrucache.h>

clru_init(name, capacity, getter, setter, evict_cb);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls clrucache_create_full() and assigns the result to name. It takes the
key type and the value type from the companion variables that
clru_declare() creates. It calls ccol_fatal_err() when the creation fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name       Cache variable. Declare it with clru_declare or
           clru_declare_scoped first
capacity   The maximum number of live entries before eviction
getter     Remote getter callback, or NULL
setter     Remote setter callback, or NULL
evict_cb   Eviction callback, or NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
This macro calls ccol_fatal_err() when an allocation fails.
Call clrucache_create_full() directly when you must handle an error
yourself.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
clru_declare(cache, int, double);
clru_init(cache, 64, NULL, NULL, NULL);
clru_destroy(cache);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clru_declare (3),
.BR clru_construct (3),
.BR clrucache_create_full (3)
